proof.text:
For a representative $u:T_{im}x\to T_{jm}y$, write $B_m^\Phi(u)=b_{jm,y}^{-1}\Phi_m(u)b_{im,x}$ and $B_m^\Psi(u)=c_{jm,y}^{-1}\Psi_m(u)c_{im,x}$. The compatibility assumed for $\eta$ and its ordinary naturality at $u$ give the three-line equality
$$U_{jm}(\eta_{j,y})B_m^\Phi(u)=c_{jm,y}^{-1}\eta_{m,T_{jm}y}\Phi_m(u)b_{im,x}
=c_{jm,y}^{-1}\Psi_m(u)\eta_{m,T_{im}x}b_{im,x}
=B_m^\Psi(u)U_{im}(\eta_{i,x}).$$
Using step 5 and composition at stage $m$ [def-sf-directed-common-stage-data], this is precisely the naturality square for $[m,u]$. Every arrow has a representative, so the components define $\overline\eta$.
